<title>JAPAN: Shiseido lifted as investors seek laggards.</title>
<headline>Shiseido lifted as investors seek laggards.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Shiseido Co Ltd rose on Wednesday as investors sought domestic laggards rather than the international blue chips which had been bought aggressively in recent weeks, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0442 GMT, the shares were 30 yen higher at 1,570. Turnover totaled 5.966 million shares, making Shiseido the second most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
</text>
